<div id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The next code snippet demonstrates an example of an <span id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Infeasible Input</span> taken from the <span id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">textrank</span> project.
The below <span id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">Go</span> function inserts a value into the map <span id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">ranks.SentenceMap</span> (respectively, <span id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">ranks.sentence_map</span> for the <span id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">Rust</span> translation).
<span id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MatchFixAgent</span> discovers that these functions return different values when the map is initially <span id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">{ 1 : ‘‘SomeString’’ }</span> (the <span id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">Go</span> returns 0 while the <span id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">Rust</span> returns 1).
However, when the <span id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">textrank</span> is used properly via its public interface, this initial state for the map cannot occur.
The map will always contain keys from <math id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of map entries. Under this precondition, the functions are equivalent.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_listing" style="width:163.9pt;"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx15" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#666666;">——————-<span id="lstnumberx15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span></span>GO<span id="lstnumberx15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>SOURCE<span id="lstnumberx15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span>CODE<span id="lstnumberx15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space"> </span><span id="lstnumberx15.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#666666;">——————-</span>
</div>
